note as CONTEXT_CONTRACT_diagram_45_system_context
  SYSTEM CONTEXT CONTRACT
  - UK: system_context_versions(context, version_number).
  - current_version_id must point to a version owned by the same context.
  - Every input is snapshotted by source identity, version/hash and freshness.
  - Secrets are never stored in context_json; only governed references are allowed.
end note

note as ENUM_CONTRACT_diagram_45_system_context
  DYNAMIC ENUM CONTRACT
  Dynamic enums are NOT PostgreSQL ENUM types. A definition points to a
  terminology.value_set; each published version snapshots ordered concept options.
  Resolution considers effective time, tenant, country and optional system context,
  preserving historical validation while allowing values to change without deploys.
end note

note as POLY_diagram_45_system_context
  POLYMORPHIC REFERENCES
  system_context_inputs and system_context_bindings use governed discriminators.
  Validate schema/entity/consumer types against system_ops.entity_registry and
  closed terminology value sets before accepting a reference.
end note

note as DEP_diagram_45_system_context
  Connects to other modules via:
  terminology.value_sets/value_set_versions/catalog_concepts,
  health_context.country_health_context_versions, directory.tenants and iam.users.
end note


